江与环 The River and the Ring — Transit Map (地铁线路图), a NEO-Cine library demo

An unofficial fan film about a real metro. It is not made, endorsed or checked by Guangzhou Metro Group (广州地铁集团)
or any operator, and shows no operator logo, lettering or official map. The numbered discs are generic line bullets.
Line colours, line numbers and station names are public facts. Every date and figure on screen is sourced in FACTS.md.
Trains are illustrative: they shuttle on the opened track at an invented pace, not on a real timetable (said on the
last card).

STYLE: adapted from Lemo-Opuscar's Transit Map (MIT, (c) 2026 LemoLab; licence text in LICENSES/lemo-opuscar-MIT.txt):
  demo/film.js, demo/gl.js, demo/tools/subset.py and the net.js format are adapted from its demo/ (the MIT notice is kept
  in their headers). What NEO-Cine changed is listed at the top of each file and in ../STYLE.md.
  The style's later refinements borrow the general grammar of minimalist transit-puzzle games (bold lines, hand-dragged
  growth, springy interchanges, running trains, tuned notes); no game's design, icons, palette, typeface, sounds or music
  are copied.

MAP DATA: (c) OpenStreetMap contributors, Open Database License (ODbL) 1.0. https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright
  Fetched 2026-11-13 through the Overpass API:
  - data/metro.json: neo/geo/routes.py, route=subway|light_rail|monorail relations of the networks 广州地铁 and 广佛 in
    113.15-113.85 E, 22.55-23.65 N (19 metro lines; the trams are left out). Line 3's Airport South station, missing
    from OSM, is added by tools/prep.py between Gaozeng and Airport North.
  - data/water.json: neo/geo/osm.py, waterway centre lines, slimmed by tools/prep.py to the named Pearl River channels.
  These are derived databases and stay under ODbL 1.0. The film is a produced work and credits OpenStreetMap on its
  last card.
  The map is a schematic: tools/prep.py keeps the real topology, station order and the published line colours (OSM
  colour tags) and lays the network out on eight directions (net.js); it is our own drawing, not the operator's map.
  Water is drawn as bands; every pair of neighbouring stations is checked against the real track for which channel it
  crosses. View: the city region only; no national, provincial or other boundary is fetched or drawn.

FACTS: see FACTS.md (Guangzhou Metro Group chronicles and company profile, gz.gov.cn, Yangcheng Evening News,
  Guangzhou Daily, Science and Technology Daily, China Daily, The Paper, ifeng). Checked 2026-11-13.

PICTURE: drawn entirely in code (Canvas 2D ink, WebGL2 paper, light and depth of field). No photographs, scans,
  AI-generated images, video or 3D models.

SOUND: all synthesized for this film in mix.py: tuned station notes (marimba, glass bell and vibraphone voices in
  numpy; kalimba, music box, harp and nylon-string voices by the library's core/audio/pluck.py), pad, snaps, pops,
  ticks, felt-tip glide and distant rail sounds through core/audio/sfx.py. No samples or recordings.

FONTS (SIL Open Font License 1.1; fetched by tools/fonts.sh from github.com/google/fonts at commit 86aced91, not kept in
  git; licence texts in fonts/):
- Inter (variable, Inter[opsz,wght].ttf), The Inter Project Authors: Latin text and figures.
- Noto Sans SC (variable, NotoSansSC[wght].ttf), Google / Adobe: Chinese text, subset by tools/subset.py to the
  characters the film prints (fonts/NotoSansSC-sub.ttf).

TOOLS: the NEO-Cine library's core/ tools, which are Lemo-Opuscar's (MIT, (c) 2026 LemoLab): headless Chrome frame
  capture, events export, reading-time check, ffmpeg encode and loudness master; neo/geo/routes.py, neo/geo/osm.py,
  neo/audio/cues.py, neo/audio/master.py, neo/render/remote.sh.
